st the value reconstructed for the control by the same loader arithmetic (ceil(296334/32) = 9261) and treats `env` as the schema's environment block (control values reconstructed from the exp_01 record; `PYTHONHASHSEED` excluded as already specified). (A6, 2026-09-12 18:4x, from the Fable round-3b review, finding 2) `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` is excluded from the control-parity diff: the device index is not a recipe parameter (both cards are identical RTX A6000s; exp_01's control trained on GPU 1), and the treatment trains on whichever card the launcher is given (`--gpu`), recorded in `effective_args.json`; §5/§7's `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0` is read as `<gpu>`. (A7, same time, finding 3) Finalisation policy: after the child exits the launcher re-hashes the genuinely mutable inputs strictly (`effective_args.json`, `train_manifest.json`, the control's `args.json`, the bound probe receipt, the training-split inventory) but compares the source closures against the immutable `reviewed_blob_sha256` recorded at spawn; working-tree drift of closure files after spawn cannot affect the running interpreter and is recorded in `completion.json` as `source_drift_after_spawn` instead of aborting; a `finalize <attempt_dir>` mode re-runs output validation → revalidation → completion → promotion for a preserved attempt once the child's process group is gone and the log sink is closed. (A8, same time, finding 10) The 43 h cumulative ceiling of §7 counts `full` attempts only; smoke and probe attempts are recorded in `cumulative_hours.json` with their mode but not summed. (A9, 2026-09-12 19:0x, from the Coder's round-4 report) The approved closure digests (evaluator, manifest writer, launchers, producers) are NOT stored inside `tools/exp04_profiles.py` — the producers import that module, so its own digest would be circular — but in a committed, runtime-read JSON `worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_04_yaw_aug_xrir_claude/yaw_aug_xrir_results_assets/approved_digests.json` (not imported, hence outside ev