    exp_05 record: an archived ancestor may carry the products too
    
    `ckpt/exp05` is the natural unit to archive, and it holds the products as well as
    the arms, so "any ancestor of an attempt may be a directory symlink" has to be
    true of `results/` too.  It was not: `record.load` identified a product by its
    resolved path, and `make_figures` resolved its sources before handing them over,
    so behind a symlink both refused the published sidecar's own output coverage --
    red on a fresh `collect`, on `check_record` and on redrawing a figure, with no
    byte changed.  A product is now read at the name its sidecar gives it, which is
    the name the binder already binds.
    
    `make_figures` keeps resolving for the two questions that are about files rather
    than names: duplicate `--curve` inputs, and the device/inode preflight of every
    predicted destination.  The README gains the archiving rule the migration needs.
    
