Exp_03 is complete and committed. Here is where things stand.

**Result.** The claim that jointly rotating the panorama and the source–receiver coordinates in yaw substantially degrades xRIR is **not supported**, for the same-budget SimpleViT model and for the released checkpoint alike. No cell reaches the pre-registered +10 % threshold, and every adjusted query-level upper bound for EDT and C50 stays below it (largest +7.56 %). The measured effect is a few per cent of C50 error at ±22.5° to ±45° and about zero at 180° and ±5.6°, a pattern consistent with a distribution shift at diagonal headings (all training rooms are axis-aligned). The alignment step contributes nothing measurable (condition E equals P to 2e-5). The cylindrical backbone does not degrade less; its tokens are equivariant but the learned position pool and the absolute-coordinate embeddings, shared by both backbones, are the candidate sources of the residual. The properly paired k = 0 comparison gives the cylindrical model a 4.4 % lower EDT with both query-level and room-cluster intervals excluding zero, and no C50 difference.

**Commits on main.** `4131f7d` (the whole record: plan with amendment history, parameters, exact command record, per-action notebook, results.md and page generated only from the canonical JSON, analysis with residual limitations and open tooling items, gate decisions, all logs, eight Codex review rounds, provenance tooling, 32 adversarial tests) and `19a04ef` (commits file). Ten producer commits from the Coder precede them. The unrelated exp_01/exp_02 commits-file edits remain uncommitted.

**Review outcome and a decision you may want to revisit.** The Codex reviewer confirmed in round 8 that the evidence path is sound (numbers, verdicts, canonical artefacts, bindings, and an acceptance checker that recomputes the gate decision byte-for-byte from the bound inputs). Its verdict nonetheless stayed "request changes" on auxiliary tooling items, and each round produced new edge cases. I recorded a decision rule in the notebook and committed once the evidence path was confirmed; the open items are listed verbatim in the analysis (launcher v3 not certified for a clean re-run, renderer corruption edge cases, non-crash-atomic binder). If you prefer the loop to continue, those items are the starting point.

**Residual limitations disclosed in the analysis.** All provenance binding is post hoc, five gate commands are reconstructed, the launcher was never used for a real run, and CUDA nondeterminism is unquantified. None requires a rerun.

Recommended next steps are in the analysis: yaw augmentation if heading robustness matters, hold-one-fixed ablations of the pool and coordinate branches, and a second training seed before quoting the EDT advantage at room level.
